Subject: [PATCH 1/2] on a crash, kill only this evaluator's own CARLA

Safety fix. On "Simulation crashed" the evaluator ran

    ps -ef | grep '-graphicsadapter=<gpu_rank>' | ... | xargs -r kill -9

which kills every CARLA server on that GPU that the same Unix user can signal,
not just the one this evaluator launched. On a machine with one GPU that is
every CARLA the user runs: parallel sweep workers, a second gate lane, a
colleague's job under a shared service account. One crashed route took all of
them down.

The server this evaluator owns is already known: `_setup_simulation` launches
it with `preexec_fn=os.setsid`, so its process group is exactly that server and
its children. Killing that group is what the crash handler needs. No setting
reaches this code, so it has to be a patch.

Should go upstream.

diff --git a/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py b/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py
index 2f91b57..0958f7d 100644
--- a/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py
+++ b/leaderboard/leaderboard/leaderboard_evaluator.py
@@ -498,9 +498,14 @@ class LeaderboardEvaluator(object):
             self.statistics_manager.validate_and_write_statistics(self.sensors_initialized, crashed)
         
         if crashed:
-            cmd2 = "ps -ef | grep '-graphicsadapter="+ str(args.gpu_rank) + "' | grep -v grep | awk '{print $2}' | xargs -r kill -9"
-            server = subprocess.Popen(cmd2, shell=True, preexec_fn=os.setsid)
-            atexit.register(os.killpg, server.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
+            # Only this evaluator's own CARLA: its server runs in a session of its
+            # own (setsid above), so its process group is exactly that server.
+            # Matching every '-graphicsadapter=N' process killed each CARLA the
+            # same user ran on that GPU, parallel workers' included.
+            try:
+                os.killpg(self.server.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
+            except ProcessLookupError:
+                pass
 
         return crashed
 
